    <Placemark>
      <name>Turmoil and Triumph: Art through the War Years</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Turmoil and Triumph: Art through the War Years</b><br><i>Arts &amp; Culture</i><br>Tue 12th May – Fri 17th Jul<br>Alon Zakaim Fine Art, London<br>Check site<br><br>focussed on the First World War, the interwar period, and the Second World War, a chronological and thematic exploration of the relationship between conflict and artistic transformation<br><br><a href="https://www.galleriesnow.net/shows/turmoil-and-triumph-art-through-the-war-years/">More info / tickets</a>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#orange-dot.png</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-0.141225,51.510532,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Isabelle Young: Venice As I Was</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Isabelle Young: Venice As I Was</b><br><i>Arts &amp; Culture</i><br>Tue 12th May – Fri 3rd Jul<br>Canopy Collections, London<br>Check site<br><br>the British photographer’s first exhibition with the gallery - &quot;Young’s Venice is both elegy and diary. The city appears suspended at the threshold of submergence … both shielded and already defeated&quot; - Alona Pardo<br><br><a href="https://www.galleriesnow.net/shows/isabelle-young-venice-as-i-was/">More info / tickets</a>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#orange-dot.png</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-0.091455,51.474214,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Jason Shulman: Moving Pictures</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<b>Jason Shulman: Moving Pictures</b><br><i>Arts &amp; Culture</i><br>Wed 13th May – Sat 4th Jul<br>Ashley Saville, London<br>Check site<br><br>“Shulman is a romantic artist. His themes – loss, memory, nostalgia, death, the porous membrane between joy and pain, time and space, forgetting and remembering, would be familiar to the poet, John Keats” - Nicola Shulman<br><br><a href="https://www.galleriesnow.net/shows/jason-shulman-moving-pictures/">More info / tickets</a>]]></description>
      <styleUrl>#orange-dot.png</styleUrl>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>0.04765,51.501882,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
